# E4 on far food (pheromones lane; Reports/brain-training/evolvable-pheromones-2026-10-25.md §9.15; Scott chose
# "Repeat it 6 times on runners" 2026-10-28 13:30Z). pf4w's set-up exactly (same ref, bed, operator, 40 generations),
# replicates R=1..6 at SEED=100+R, split over two batches (e4a: R=1-3, e4b: R=4-6) so it holds 6 of the 20 shared
# runner slots, not 10. Verdict fixed before launch: garden.py over all twelve (SCORE=heaphome PATCHES=20000:100:250
# DEAFALSO=A,B, PP_BED_W=448, one local build of this ref), its rule unchanged: SIGNALS FORM if >= 3/6 free bests meet
# criteria 1-3 (deaf/shift/const each lower by >= 20% on >= 12/16) and free/deaf geomean >= 0.90; DEAD END if 0/6;
# else INCONCLUSIVE. Second question, also fixed now: the signalling arm forages better if free stage B > its paired
# deaf in 6/6 (sign test p = 0.031); 5/6 (p = 0.22) is not a result.
